 ],
 "says": "A person founds a Team alone, renames it once (so it holds two profile versions, Platform and Platform standards) and closes it with a plan naming themselves as the surviving owner. On the closed Team they then recover its evidence three times through the Team's retention authority (team.retention.apply recover_evidence), each naming exact evidence digests: purpose read of the first profile version, answered as a preview that writes nothing and returns the closed team_state; purpose preserve of the renamed profile, committed under its own receipt and returning the same closed team_state; and purpose clean_up of the first profile version, committed likewise. A final team.state.read at the head the last recovery moved to returns the closed team_state, the renamed profile, and the unchanged policy, membership and grant. The recoveries name only those two profile digests and never the policy or grant, and no step writes a team_state other than closed: nothing reopens or restores the Team.",
 "spec_sha256": "e1606bff5a6ef9f3faa8a119ce2a6d97c4fd976715d0854ad8db0205c1b8cbb9",
